[Music]  i'm mark bustos and i'm going to go over  five tips on using the blow dryer  tip number one is not to hold the blow  dryer too close to the hair  you want to hold the blow dryer about  six to eight inches away from the  hairline drying  one reason for that is you don't want to  burn your own head and two you don't  want to burn the hair  very simple tip number two on using the  blow dryer is  not keeping the heat on the hair for too  long once the hair has been completely  dried you're pretty much done  because if you leave the heat on the  hair for too long again you're going to  burn the hair and you're going to dry it  out  so once it's completely dry that's it  pull away  tip number three on using a blow dryer  use the pressure of the blow dryer to  push the hair in the direction you want  to wear it a lot of times the big  mistake i see people doing with the blow  dryer  probably just go like this  you can already see the frizziness  starting to take place and do the hair  so if you want to wear your hair over to  the right and smooth it out to the right  put the concentrator on and direct the  pressure of the air  in the direction you want to wear the  hair and if you don't have a brush you  can totally just use your fingers and  kind of give it a little bit of a tug  so tip number four is using the blow  dryer to increase or decrease volume  you can use the blow dryer to do either  one so if i wanted to be a slightly  flatter into the back area over here  and a little bit higher and through here  all i'm really going to do is use the  pressure of the blow dryer to push the  hair down  and as i work to the front i'm going to  lift the hair  up and out of the root to increase some  volume see the profile  you can see that all this hair has been  pressed down and this hair up here has  been  volumized tip number five is knowing the  hot and cold settings on the blow dryer  just like your skin and when you're hot  and you're cold  your pores open and close if you look at  an individual hair under a microscope  the outer coating of the hair called the  cuticle will look like shingles on a  roof  so once you put the hot air on the  cuticle or shingles it'll open up the  cubicle  and you'll be able to manipulate the  hair and move it into whatever direction  you want to wear it and once you've  gotten the hair completely dry  you hit it with the cold air and it'll  shut the cuticle of the hair and  kind of seal it and keep it in place the  cold air will also shut the cuticle  which in turn will make your hair nice  and shiny and healthy  now that we've blown it into place you  can really just use a minimal amount of  product to keep it in place

